      "math_academy_id": "q-38880",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[T(x)]_{B}$, given that\n$\\,$ $[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "The image of $[x]_{B}$ relative to the basis $B$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{B} & =[T]_{B}[x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
